IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `au-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `au-part1-application`

-- Tests for Part 1. Expected values are written from the text.

#ASSERT `the short title of this Act` EQUALS "Acts Interpretation Act 1901"
-- Endnote 3: Acts Interpretation Act 1901, No 2 of 1901, assent 12 July 1901, commencement 12 July 1901.
#ASSERT `the day this Act was assented to` EQUALS YMD 1901 7 12
#ASSERT `the day this Act commenced` EQUALS YMD 1901 7 12
-- 12 July 1901 was a Friday.
#ASSERT NOT (`is weekend` (`the day this Act was assented to`))
-- 2(1) and (2): the Act applies unless a contrary intention appears.
#ASSERT `a provision of this Act applies to the Act or provision` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`a provision of this Act applies to the Act or provision` TRUE)
-- 2A.
#ASSERT `this Act binds the Crown in each of its capacities`
-- This Act's own default (s 3A(2)) is not what applied to itself: it names its own commencement day (endnote 3).
#ASSERT `the day the enactment commences` `Act` (`commencement on a particular day` (`the day this Act commenced`)) (`the day this Act was assented to`) EQUALS JUST (YMD 1901 7 12)
